{"document":3,"title":"user in #4bc144e2:d75245ea: I'm planning a trip to Orlando, FL and was wonderi...","updated_at":"2023-05-24T08:50:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"Getting to Universal Studios Florida from your hotel is relatively easy, with several options available. Here are a few: **Universal's SuperStar Shuttle:** 1. **Free Shuttle:** If you're staying at one of Universal's on-site hotels, you can use their complimentary shuttle service, which runs regularly throughout the day. 2. **Off-Site Hotels:** Some off-site hotels also offer shuttle services to Universal Studios Florida. Check with your hotel to see if they offer this service and what the schedule is. **Uber and Lyft:** 1. **Ride-Sharing:** You can use Uber or Lyft to get to Universal Studios Florida from your hotel. This is a convenient option, especially if you're traveling with a group or prefer a more direct route. 2. **Cost:** The cost of an Uber or Lyft ride will depend on the time of day, traffic, and your hotel's location. Expect to pay around $10-$20 per ride, depending on the distance. **Taxis:** 1. **Taxi Service:** You can also take a taxi from your hotel to Universal Studios Florida. This is a good option if you prefer a more traditional transportation method. 2. **Cost:** The cost of a taxi ride will depend on the distance and traffic. Expect to pay around $15-$30 per ride. **Driving and Parking:** 1. **Self-Parking:** If you have a car, you can drive to Universal Studios Florida and park in their parking garage. Self-parking costs around $25 per day. 2. **Preferred Parking:** If you want to park closer to the theme park entrance, you can upgrade to preferred parking for around $40 per day. **Other Options:** 1. **Hotel Shuttles:** Some hotels offer shuttle services to Universal Studios Florida, so be sure to check with your hotel to see if they offer this service.\n2. **Public Transportation:** You can also use public transportation, such as buses, to get to Universal Studios Florida. This is a more affordable option, but may take longer. Remember to plan your transportation in advance, especially during peak seasons or special events, to ensure you arrive at the theme park on time.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"4bc144e2:d75245ea\"}"}
